{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added a per-feed `fetch_timeout` (integer seconds, 0 = use the global timeout). Existing unit and integration tests pass; the new behaviour itself is not exercised by them.\n\n- **Schema**: new migration adds `feeds.fetch_timeout int not null default 0`.\n- **Model / API**: `fetch_timeout` is on the feed object and accepted by `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}` via `FeedModificationRequest` and `Patch`.\n- **Storage**: the column is read in the feed query and written in `CreateFeed` and `UpdateFeed`.\n- **Refresh**: `RefreshFeed` uses the per-feed value when it is > 0, otherwise `HTTPClientTimeout()`.\n- **Client package**: `Feed.FetchTimeout` and `FeedModificationRequest.FetchTimeout` added.\n\nThings to know:\n- The validator rejects negative values and values above 86400 with the key `error.feed_invalid_fetch_timeout`. I did not add translations for that key, so the message will show as the raw key unless they are added.\n- The override applies only to the feed refresh fetch. Feed creation, icon fetching and the scraper still use the global timeout.\n- `fetch_timeout` is not accepted on feed creation, and there is no field for it in the web UI's feed edit form.", "t": 1794464008.986}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794464008.986}
